From 0c6ce26cebd66bea74187f6107129262af6f3610 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xander Burchartz <210020462+xanderburchartz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:50:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] iOS: touch input on the chart canvas

Chart canvas, toolbar, compass and piano for a touch screen:

- Pinch zoom through wxZoomGestureEvent and long press from the iOS touch
  filter in the app layer; drag inertia with a cap.
- Retina scaling in the GL path; widgets kept clear of the rounded screen
  corners.
- No wxClientDC outside paint events (crashes under wxQt).
- Actions that were only in the menu bar (iOS has none) are added to the
  context menu.

The iOS implementation lives in the iOS app layer (app/ios/*_ios.cpp in the
opencpn-ios repository); the core only declares and calls it.

All changes are inside #ifdef __OCPN__IOS__; other platforms are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
